Subject: [PATCH 6/6] grate: complete draws before releasing their jobs

Draw jobs are submitted immediately and released, without tracking their
fences on resources. A later context flush sees an empty stream, and the
resource transfer-map path maps memory without waiting for outstanding
draws. CPU readback and gr2d clears can therefore race a gr3d draw.

Wait in the draw submission path as a correctness-first fallback until
resource fence tracking is implemented. The existing stream wait has its
result checked and errors are logged. This serializes rendering and is
not a performance optimization.

Applies after 0005. Validate with original rotating cube shaders, depth
on, and no GRATE_DRM_WAIT environment override. Isolated raster/depth
pixel differences are a separate unresolved issue.

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/grate/grate_draw.c b/src/gallium/drivers/grate/grate_draw.c
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/grate/grate_draw.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/grate/grate_draw.c
@@ -408,7 +408,14 @@
 
    grate_stream_end(stream, &ptr);
 
-   grate_stream_flush(stream, false);
+   /* Draws are submitted immediately, but resource maps and context flushes
+    * do not track/wait their fences yet. Complete the draw before releasing
+    * its job so CPU readback and subsequent gr2d clears cannot race it.
+    * Replace this synchronous fallback with resource fence tracking later.
+    */
+   err = grate_stream_flush(stream, true);
+   if (err < 0)
+      grate_loge("grate_stream_flush() failed: %d\n", err);
 }
 
 void
